Z||000000||DreXteR||08-09-2001||02:37 PM||||I need to pick a perfect choice of pistons rings for my setup. I will using forged pistons .030 over, the aplication will be forced induction(high boost). Now, need to know what look for and price wise. As far I have now is Total Seal or Seal Power for $96.  <P>Need advice!!!!!!!!<P>Thanx<P><BR>DreX||||reg||5
Z||000001||DreXteR||08-09-2001||02:51 PM||||Update .. . . .. . . . <P>Call again and the type of rings needed for my application will be TS1 and price is $144.63 !!!! OUCH!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> <P>There is another option???<P><BR>Thanx<P><BR>DreX<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Capt Fiero||08-09-2001||02:54 PM||||Well you pretty well nailed it right on the head, the total seal gapless rings are the best on the market.  I am not sure if you can get them in the chrom-moly but when I did my engine I did not get the total seal due to price and I did find a set of the chrom rings, acording to my engine builder the chrome rings will probably outlast the cylnder walls.  Thas one of 2 things that I did to make my motor better over all, the other was using roller tip rockers to save the valve seals and guides from premature wear.<P>------------------<BR>David<BR>85GT<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://photos.onebigvillage.com/pubimage.asp?id_=32415"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||DreXteR||08-09-2001||09:59 PM||||Top||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black88GT||08-09-2001||10:23 PM||||Capt Fiero, I was wondering how roller tip rockers save the valve seals and guides from premature wear.||||reg||1
Z||000005||V8Dreamer||08-10-2001||10:05 AM||||Well, I have the moly rings in my 86 2.5.........and all I can say is DON'T BEAT IT RIGHT AWAY!!!!!  My car was beaten on about 1 min after it was fired up after the rebuild and now, about 20k later, it's like driving a 2stroke lawnmower......at least the bugs don't bother me though....it's just stopping at lights that sucks, when the stink catches up with you.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DreXteR||08-10-2001||10:18 AM||||V8Dreamer what you are try to say is that get the a good set of rings???  Dont try to be cheap on these parts??<P>DreX||||reg||5
Z||000007||Phaeton||08-11-2001||02:34 AM||||The rocker arm scrubs across the top of the valve when going down, creating a side load on the valvestem.  Not enough to make much of a difference even  with high miles.<P>When I couldn't afford full rollers I used cast roller tips just for the mental horsepower.  Worth every cent and I would do it again.||||reg||12
